<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-adams-gallery-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The earliest documents held in this collection: two messages sent within about twenty minutes of each other on the evening of 2008-08-08 to the Ansel Adams organisation, one carrying eight loose photographs of the print and one carrying the archive later sent to the auction house. They precede the museum letter by two days and the auction house by five, and they identify the body that letter miscalls the Ansel Adams Museum in San Francisco. The message carrying the archive retains its original Hotmail headers; the other has been rewritten by a later platform, and their relative order is not settled." .
