<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-archived-websites-2013-2016> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The Internet Archive holds dated captures of two domains the studio ran, and those captures are public and checkable by anyone. On www.wtfisart.com: a capture of 2013-07-20 showing only 'Under Construction:Check back soon !', and captures of 2014-12-18 and 2016-01-11 showing a site whose menu reads 'Artists', 'Art Market Reform is a happening' and 'Got Provenance ?', and whose text reads 'For the Love of God, We are the Art. Long Live the Art Spirit !', alongside the phrases 'Art is Capital invest with confidence' and 'What Hedge Funds ?! invest in Art'. On www.sunandrainworks.com: captures of 2016-01-26 and 2016-03-27 carrying the eight defining characteristics of Metaconceptual Art in full, in the same wording as the 2012 posting recorded elsewhere in this collection. What these captures establish is that the concept, its eight characteristics, and the studio's art-market vocabulary were published on the studio's own domains and preserved by a third party on dates no one in the studio controls. What they do not establish is anything about the auction of 2009: no capture mentions it, or lot 16, or Ansel Adams, or Sotheby's." .
