<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-agreement-2009> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The executed consignment agreement between Sotheby's, Inc. and the studio principal for the sale of 30 March 2009, together with the two emails that carried it. On 2009-03-18 the administrator of the Photographs department sent a scanned PDF of the agreement, writing that a signed agreement was required before the photograph could be sold. On 2009-03-19 the studio returned a signed PDF as an attachment named 'JoeArtChirum.pdf', with a covering note hoping the electronic format was suitable. That file is held. It runs to seven scanned pages: a six-page agreement on Sotheby's letterhead, dated 18-Mar-2009, addressed to the studio principal, naming Sotheby's principal auctioneer, carrying the consignor's signature above the line 'Consignor - Accepted and agreed' and a countersignature for Sotheby's, Inc.; and one further page of identity verification. This is the instrument of consignment itself, and the point at which the consignment ceases to be an inference from correspondence. Neither the document nor its terms are published here, for two independent reasons set out below." .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-agreement-2009> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P1_is_identified_by> _:r12b0 .
