<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-facebook-2009> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "On 2009-12-19 at 16:13:43 UTC, by Facebook's clock, the studio principal wrote in a private Facebook message, replying to a musician who had asked whether they knew each other: 'I live between Eugene, and Kaua'i, and am a meta-conceptual artist, and musician, doing my part to help furthur Art History.' It is the earliest dated use of any form of the term Metaconceptual Art in this collection: nine months after the Sotheby's sale, and one year and eleven months before the public posting of 2011-11-28 that had been the earliest located use. In the same month the studio captioned two of its own photographs, uploaded to its Facebook albums, with wordplay on art: a Kaua'i paint shop trading under a 'Pittsburgh Paints' sign, uploaded on 2009-12-01 at 04:38:28 UTC as 'Artists who know, paint with only the finest... Kaua'i meets Pittsburgh !!!', and a Kilauea paint shop and shave-ice stand, uploaded on 2009-12-30 at 03:32:17 UTC as 'What art ?'. The studio states that the wordplay was by design." .
