<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-facebook-2018> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Three public Facebook comments by the studio principal on 2018-10-11, at times Facebook assigns, on posts by the art publications ARTnews and Artsy. At 22:06:32 UTC, on the ARTnews post: 'I auctioned Lot 16 of Sotheby's May 2009 photography auction as a live performance Contemporary Metaconceptual Art piece, but that was ancient history. I'm in the catalog as the seller, listed as Anonymous, Ladies and Gentleman...' At 22:12:03 UTC, replying to that comment: 'My newly created work was titled \"WTF is Ansel Adams ?!\" 2009', with a link to the studio's public posting of 2012-11-22. At 22:24:38 UTC, on the Artsy post: 'I created Metaconceptual Art around 2008, and auctioned Lot 16 of Sotheby's May 2009 photography auction as a live Metaconceptual Performance piece. Sorry Banksy, set the stage for you 10 years ago.', with the same link. The second is the earliest use of the title 'WTF is Ansel Adams ?!' held in this collection whose date was fixed by a party other than the studio." .
