<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-facebook-message-2010> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A private Facebook message, sent by the studio principal on 2010-04-12 at 10:02:24 UTC to an old friend, in reply to the friend's question about what kind of art he was making. The part of it that bears on this collection reads, in his words: 'One of the highlights of my art career so far has been, tapping into the NY Art scene, when i auctioned off an o.g. Ansel Adams photograph of SanFrancisco from 1946 ? At Sotheby's spring photograph sale in May of 2009. I executed this art, as an act of contemporary conceptual art. It brought in a tidy sum.' The same message says he had spent the last two winters in Hawai'i, on Maui and Kaua'i, and was living in Eugene, Oregon. It is the earliest dated statement in this collection that the 2009 sale was itself a work of art: thirteen months after the sale, and three years and five months before the letter of 2013-09-12 to a university art museum, which had until now been the earliest." .
