<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-hawaii-notebook-2008-2009> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Six photographs, held by the studio only as copies downloaded from Facebook: two of pages in a handwritten notebook, and four landscapes. The first notebook photograph shows a two-page spread of drafts of a poem. The left page carries two versions, the second headed 'The Art World' and signed J.M.C.; the right page carries dated entries of 10/21/09, 10/22/09 and 10/24/2009, the last placed at Moloa'a on Kaua'i and a fair copy headed 'The Art World is Flat', followed by further, heavily revised drafts. The second shows a single page inscribed '\"The more you want, the less you have\" Joe M. Chirum 11/10/2008, Kipahulu, Maui', and beneath it a second line, in the same ink, signed 'JDawg'. The four landscapes show a rainbow over red cliffs, a rainbow over the open sea seen from a hillside, sea cliffs above a beach, and swimmers in a lava-rock tide pool. The studio states that they were taken in Hawai'i and belong to the material of WTF is Ansel Adams. The notebook's last draft of 'The Art World is Flat' is, line for line, the poem the studio posted publicly on 28 November 2011 as 'a metaconceptual Art poem i wrote a few years ago'. The pages therefore show that poem being worked out, under a date the writer gave it himself." .
