<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-hosting-receipts-2009> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A domain registrar's billing record for the studio's account, held as the registrar's own comma-separated export for 2009 together with forty-two PDF invoices, running from 2009-01-04 to 2016-01-05. It shows that on 2009-03-16 at 00:45:06 UTC the account registered the domain WTFISART.COM, on receipt 158832568, for $1.99 plus a $0.20 ICANN fee; that at 01:07:15 UTC the same night it bought 'Economy Classic Hosting Linux' for wtfisart.com at $4.99, on receipt 158833357; and that the hosting was then paid for monthly, at $4.99 with a zero-rated bandwidth line, on 2009-04-15, 2009-05-15, 2009-06-15, 2009-07-25, 2009-08-15, 2009-09-15, 2009-10-15, 2009-11-15 and 2009-12-15. In the same transaction as the domain registration the account also bought an 'Economy Quick Blogcast' for $9.98, which was refunded at 01:20:25 UTC that night on receipt 158832568R, thirty-five minutes after purchase. Separately the account registered GROWINGALOHA.COM on 2009-01-04 and renewed it on 2010-01-05. This is a third party's business record of the studio's account, and it dates the domain and its hosting from fourteen days before the Sotheby's sale of 30 March 2009. The invoices continue past that first year under a second account number, and the paragraphs below set out what they add: the re-registration of WTFISART.COM in 2011, the registration of METACONCEPTUALART.COM in the same order, and renewals running to 2016." .
