<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-meta-sign-2012> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "One digital photograph, held by the studio, of an illuminated shop sign photographed at night. The sign carries a red oval with the word META in white capitals, with a grave accent on the final letter, and beneath it the word SUPERNEGOZI; to its right, cropped by the frame, stand the large illuminated letters S, U, P. The wording is Italian: supernegozi means superstores, and meta with that accent is the Italian word for half. The camera's Exif records the capture as 2012-02-27 21:41:53, with no location data. The studio states that the photograph was taken in Italy and that it photographed the sign because the word answered to Metaconceptual Art, the movement concept it had named; that reading is the studio's account, given in 2026, and the photograph records a sign belonging to a business unconnected with the studio." .
