<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-museum-correspondence-2013> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sun & Rain Works holds an email thread of 2013-09-12 between the studio principal and the Jordan Schnitzer Museum of Art at the University of Oregon. Writing after visiting the museum earlier that day, the studio principal set out the project in his own words: that he had created a field of contemporary art called Metaconceptual Art; that 'Art Market Reform' and 'Art Tax' were Metaconceptual Art works; that his art business was named Sun & Rain Works, at which he was Chief Executive Artist; that Metaconceptual Art had eight defining characteristics, which he described as already findable publicly at that date; and that in May 2009 he had auctioned lot 16 of a Sotheby's New York photograph auction, Ansel Adams's 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks', as what he called a performance act of Metaconceptual Art. He invited the museum to distribute and share the material freely. A member of the museum's staff replied the same afternoon, thanking him and saying she would forward it to their staff. This record evidences that the term Metaconceptual Art, its attachment to named works, and the claim to the 2009 Sotheby's consignment were all set down in writing and delivered to an art institution on 2013-09-12 - thirteen years before this site published them as linked data. It is the artist's own declaration, not an independent finding, and the museum's reply is an acknowledgement of receipt only." .
