<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-outreach-screenshots-2013> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Four screenshots, held by the studio, taken on the studio principal's Mac over two days in September 2013, the same two days as the letter to a university art museum recorded in the 2013 museum-correspondence record. The first shows a discussion he had just started in a private LinkedIn group, 'Arts & Crafts Professional', under the title '\"Art Market Reform\": Promoting Art Tax on the local, state, national, and international levels to encourage and promote accountability, transparency, and regulation in the Art Market and Art World', posted as Joseph Chirum, Chief Executive Artist at Sun and Rain Works; the group's activity panel dates the post '1 minute ago'. The second, taken at midday on 13 September, shows the same browser open at the home page of Artspace, a non-profit gallery in New Haven, Connecticut, beside a Wikipedia list of contemporary art museums. The third shows the same browser open at the Sotheby's website's list of its locations worldwide. The fourth shows the studio's webmail open at a reply from the Assistant Director of the Oregon Arts Commission, the State of Oregon's arts agency, headed 'RE: Metaconceptual Art project discussion follow up' and dated in the mail client Fri, Sep 13, 2013 at 2:58 PM. The reply thanks him for sharing his work, points him to the Commission's grants for individual artists and nonprofits, and wishes him 'the best on your proposal to the White House'. Together they show the studio carrying the same declaration to a professional network and to a state arts agency, and looking up galleries and auction houses, in the same days it wrote to the museum. They are the studio's own screenshots of its own outreach, and the one reply they show is a courtesy referral." .
