<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-pastebin-2011-2012> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P129_is_about> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/eight-sentences> .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-pastebin-2011-2012> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Two public postings on the text-hosting service Pastebin, made under the account LIVINGART8 and still publicly readable, carry Metaconceptual Art before 2013. The earlier, titled 'The Art World is Flat', was posted on 2011-11-28 at 07:51:51 CDT. It presents a poem which its author introduces as a metaconceptual Art poem written some years earlier and published free to the world that day in honour of Cyber Monday 2011, and it links to a Sun & Rain Works page on Facebook. The later, titled 'MetaConceptual Art', was posted on 2012-11-22 at 23:19:57 CDT. Headed '#WTF is MetaConceptual Art ?!' and carrying the same Facebook link, it sets out 'The 8 Defining characteristics of Metaconceptual Art' as a numbered list of eight sentences. Those eight sentences are the work catalogued in this collection as Eight Sentences On Metaconceptual Art, and they agree with the published text word for word, differing only in a comma, a space, and the spelling of 'Transcendance', later normalised to 'Transcendence'. These postings establish that the term, the eight-part definition, and the studio's attachment of both to Sun & Rain Works were public and fixed in a third party's records on 2012-11-22, and that the term was already in use as a settled description on 2011-11-28." .
