<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-saturday-market-membership> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A statement made by the Eugene Saturday Market, from its own membership records, that Sun and Rain Works was a member of the market in 2005, 2006 and 2008. The studio wrote to the market on 2024-09-03 asking for access to its historical membership records and receipts; the market's general manager replied on 2024-09-06 with those three years. The Eugene Saturday Market, in Eugene, Oregon, has run weekly since 9 May 1970 and describes itself as the oldest continuously operating weekly open-air crafts market in the United States; its rule is that goods are made and sold by the person who made them. Membership is therefore vendor membership, and what the market's records attest is that a business under this name was making and selling work at its stalls in those years. This is the earliest attestation of the name Sun and Rain Works in this collection, and the only one made by a party other than the studio about a date before 2011." .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-saturday-market-membership> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P1_is_identified_by> _:r28b0 .
