<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-sfmoma-approach-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "An email of 2008-08-11 at 16:01, sent by the studio principal to the photography department of the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art, under the subject 'Ansel Adams Finds Art in SanFrancisco'. It introduces its writer as an artist living in Eugene, Oregon and sole proprietor of an art business named Sun and Rain Works; describes the recent acquisition of a previously unknown Ansel Adams photograph of San Francisco, which the writer then believed to date from 1946; states that he owns it and is researching its historical and artistic significance; reports that he is in contact with people on the Portland art scene willing to appraise it, and with a named individual at an institution he calls the Ansel Adams Museum in San Francisco; says he thought this happening might be of some interest to the museum; describes attached photographs made with a 1.3 megapixel FujiFilm camera; and closes 'For the Love of Art'. It is three days earlier than the approach to Sotheby's, carries the same subject line, and repeats its opening paragraph almost word for word. It is no longer the earliest contemporaneous document in this collection: two messages of 2008-08-08 to the Ansel Adams organisation precede it by two days. It remains the earliest contemporaneous use of the name Sun and Rain Works, which neither earlier message carries. It should not be confused with the earliest attested date for the business, which is earlier and rests on a different kind of source: a market has stated from its own membership records that the business was trading at its stalls in 2005. That statement was made in 2024 about 2005; this letter was written in 2008 and uses the name itself." .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-sfmoma-approach-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P1_is_identified_by> _:r29b0 .
