<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-staged-photographs-2008> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Seventeen digital photographs, held by the studio, that follow the framed Ansel Adams print 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks' through a sequence: a person posing at a door with a ring of keys; the same person inside a caged storage unit, lifting the print; the print presented to the camera in storage corridors and propped against the railing of a warehouse mezzanine; two frames of the stamped and annotated verso; an older man at a framing workbench taking the print out of its frame and examining it; and three exteriors of a shed and carport. The camera recorded no capture date. The files were rewritten by QuickTime 7.5.5 under Mac OS X 10.5.5 at 2008-11-25 18:56 by that computer's clock, a processing that cannot be earlier than 2008-09-15, when Mac OS X 10.5.5 was released, and they were copied into the studio's working folder on 2009-01-20 by the file system's record. They are therefore a product of the autumn of 2008, or of January 2009 at the latest: before the consignment agreement was executed and before the sale of 30 March 2009. Sun & Rain Works states that they were made by its art assistants as documentation of WTF is Ansel Adams. They were not among the photographs sent to the museum or to the auction house, and the images themselves are not published." .
