<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-wikioccupy-2011> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P138i_has_representation> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-wikioccupy-2011#visual-item> .
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-wikioccupy-2011> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Three chat logs, a private message and a photograph, all of November 2011, that record the studio principal describing his work on a website for the Occupy movement, www.wikioccupy.org, in the language of art. The earliest of the documents is a private Facebook message of 2011-11-01, sent at 17:54:55 UTC by Facebook's clock, in which the studio principal thanked a person who had liked 'the WikiOccupy page that i created', wrote 'I am the creator and admin of www.wikioccupy.org', called the project 'The Global Wiki', described himself as 'one of the key persons of the OWSGlobalWikiWorkingGroup', and gave as his contact an address at the site's own domain under the name 'Art'; the message carries a link to the wiki's home page and is signed with his own name. It does not describe the site as art. What it adds is a date fixed by Facebook, nine days before the first of the logs, for his role as the site's creator and administrator and for his use of the name 'Art'. The logs are of an Internet Relay Chat channel of an Occupy Wall Street wiki project, #owswikifarm, in which the studio principal took part under the name 'Art', and in the log of 10 November also 'ArtLight'. In the log dated 2011-11-19, of a discussion he moderated, he wrote, in this order: 'i own www.wikioccupy.org www.wikioccupywallst.org www.wikioccupywallstreet.org www.wikioccupy.com and www.wikioccupywallstreet.com'; 'as you can see i was/am very enthusiastic about the wiki occupy idea'; and 'as an act of Art'. Later in the same log he wrote of the project, 'i mean, its not like thats the only Art project in my life'. He described the site as 'happening right now, and is continuing to happen', described Sun and Rain Works as 'an Art based entity' and 'my legal entity which is my \" Art business \"', and wrote that 'the domain is currently registered through : Sun and Rain Works'. In the log of 2011-11-10 he wrote that he had 'other Art that i make also' and called himself 'simply an American Contemporary Artist, with \" Art Assistants \"'. Art is a recurring subject in what he wrote: of the roughly seven hundred lines that are his across the three logs, some forty-five mention art or artists in their text, apart from the name he used. Among them are 'Im in it for the Art !'; 'I am an Artistic visionary who has been working on this stuff for many years now. I just didn't join the movement 2 months ago.'; and an anecdote about the Grateful Dead's choice of name, 'because of their avant garde Art, and the meaning of words', followed by 'i.e. its kinda edgey like www.wikioccupy.org'. The photograph, taken with the studio's camera phone at 07:42:37 on 2011-11-16, shows a painting on paper whose subject is the site's address: 'www.' lettered in blue across the top and 'WiKioccupy.org' lettered in black beneath it. The studio states, in 2026, that it made www.wikioccupy.org as a work of Metaconceptual Art and as its part in the Occupy Wall Street movement; that the idea of a website as a work of art came from its earlier site, www.wtfisart.com; that the studio principal went by the pseudonym 'Art' throughout this period; and that he talked about art extensively in the project's chats and meetings. The site ran on MediaWiki, as its archived pages show. What the logs and the photograph show on their own is set out below: that in November 2011 the studio principal, as 'Art', described his holding of the site's domains, and the project, as art, returned to the subject of art repeatedly, and had made a painting of the site's address." .
