_:r15b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P75i_is_possessed_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r15b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E30_Right> .
_:r15b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CC BY 4.0" .
_:r15b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Evidence archive: Art Market Reform, 'WTF is Art' and Metaconceptual Art on Facebook and USA Projects (2012-2013)" .
_:r15b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r15b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r15b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r15b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "record:evidence-facebook-2012-2013" .
_:r15b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r15b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r15b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What is earlier than before, and by how much. The public comment of 2012-08-14 is the earliest dated use of the title 'Art Market Reform' held here, thirteen months before the museum letter of 2013-09-12 that had been the earliest; the private message of 2013-05-29 is the earliest calling it a work of Metaconceptual Art. The comment of 2012-11-21 is the earliest dated appearance of the phrase 'WTF is Art' with a third party's date, nine months before the X post of 2013-08-29, and one day before the public posting of 2012-11-22 headed '#WTF is MetaConceptual Art ?!'. It was written on the day the registrar's receipts show ARTMARKETREFORM.ORG being registered, and a few hours after the comment that calls Art Market Reform profanity. The message of 2012-11-25 is the earliest dated naming of 'Art Historians from the Future', six months before the Flickr posting of the digital work on 2013-06-02. The USA Projects page is the earliest Internet Archive capture held here of a page carrying the term Metaconceptual Art of the studio's own work, on a site the studio did not run; it precedes the museum letter by a month. The public use of the term itself is older, in the posting of 2011-11-28." .
_:r15b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r15b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r15b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A message of 30 October 2012, before the definition was published. On 2012-10-30 at 15:18:13 UTC, by Facebook's clock, the studio principal wrote privately to an artist in New York whom he did not know; there was no reply: 'I had a profound to the core earth shattering \"Art Vision\" 4+ years ago, which illuminated to me the multidimensional nature of art. This was the birth of metaconceptual Art. Metaconceptual art has 8 defining characteristics, blah blah blah, its interconnected with the fabric of the Universe and it involves an interdisciplinary collaborative unification of our synergistic efforts to create the organic machinery of Living Art for the benefit of body mind and spirit of all human kind. For The Love of God, We Are the Art.' Three things in it are earlier than this collection had held. It refers to the eight defining characteristics twenty-three days before the public posting of 2012-11-22 that sets them out, though it does not list them. It is the earliest dated appearance of the line 'For the Love of God, We Are the Art', which the collection had otherwise first in a message of 2013-07-23 and in the website capture of 2014-12-18. And it places the 'Art Vision' that was 'the birth of metaconceptual Art' about four years before October 2012, that is in about 2008, where the studio's undated profile biography gives 2007. The recipient is not named. The thread's file in the account data, 2,333 bytes, has SHA-256 4f5d17de6efc3bf220792cf962eabfe7db80a70f941d6e427bd71abb05602f12, within the archive facebook-joechirum-2026-09-24-TZ87gGfq.zip, SHA-256 c978c3bd338a6a9a934d3aa05a81d2c298c49200bf7e4edc98b8329c02103097." .
_:r15b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r15b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r15b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Evidence status. The Facebook items are dated by Facebook, from the account data it compiled and delivered on request on 2026-09-24, held by the studio as facebook-joechirum-2026-09-24-TZ87gGfq.zip, SHA-256 c978c3bd338a6a9a934d3aa05a81d2c298c49200bf7e4edc98b8329c02103097. The four comments are in the export's comments file, 874,950 bytes, SHA-256 6bccd7fe8c5e3057c9fccbdcffa62519501e3e8c3585eaccd09eb914ca5249d0. The messages are in three archived threads, of 88,494, 1,200 and 4,062 bytes, with SHA-256 1d3b2a20d85b4ac622e22750db44b1e758e777a65fe505577f9f5b95a0695993, 279fa2963258dd639e10907d1f4a0918ede159891b1bd2e227ab0a425aee980e and 3c39b34bdd158d8171c26ff9eef29eff1dc19f3122023bed5fd807b588f22def. The USA Projects page is dated by the Internet Archive, which captured it at 2013-08-12 08:16:17 UTC and again on 2013-08-14, with its supporting pages on 2013-09-17, at https://web.archive.org/web/20130812081617/http://www.usaprojects.org:80/project/pittsburgh_city_of_bridges_city_of_god. The capture as retrieved on 2026-09-24, 36,818 bytes, has SHA-256 a956b435d0b40f5522bdb73a20919ba2028f14e458e02c014ffbac741f723372. USA Projects was the fundraising programme of the non-profit United States Artists; the page shows a goal of $2,500, $50 raised, and a closing date of 21 August." .
_:r15b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r15b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r15b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What these do and do not show. Every item is the studio principal's own writing; the Facebook dates and the archive's capture fix when he wrote or published it, not whether what he wrote is true. None of them concerns the 2009 sale, and none evidences the 2007 origin asserted elsewhere. The comments were made on a public figure's posts, where they could be read by others; the messages were private, and the page was public. That a phrase or title was in use by a date is all they establish, and each is recorded here for that. The later comments on the same critic's posts, 2013 to 2018. The four comments quoted above are not the whole series. The comments file holds twenty-three comments by the studio principal on the same New York art critic's public posts and photographs, from 2012-08-14 to 2018-12-02, at times Facebook assigns. Those of 2013 onward that concern the art market or the studio's titles are these: 'just as long as theres no difference between \"insider money\" and \"outsider money\" art=money #notrocketscience' (2013-02-10 16:26:00 UTC); 'must be time for #ArtMarketReform' (2013-05-25 04:25:01 UTC); 'time for \"Art Market Reform\"' (2014-02-06 18:11:12 UTC); 'Add some lovely anonymous buyers and sellers, a dash of insider trading, a teaspoon of market manipulation, a generous sprinkle of front running, money laundering to taste, and a generous helping of tax evasion. Another beautiful day in the Art World.' (2014-05-09 22:03:35 UTC); 'Art ... From the Top Down... Sounds like the end of civilization as we know it. Time for Art Market Reform. Multinational corporate money and sponsorship is not a requirement for great Art. What Hedge Funds ?!' (2015-07-30 01:10:38 UTC); 'Which candidate supports #ArtMarketReform ?!' (2016-06-22 22:06:32 UTC); 'Metaconceptual Art ?!' (2016-10-23 20:38:03 UTC); 'Spectacular theatrical market manipulation ! Bravo Ladies and Gentlemen' (2018-10-09 15:09:53 UTC); and 'Anyone in the Art world want to volunteer to start paying sales tax ?' (2018-10-18 22:36:06 UTC). The others are a question about an installation at the Hirshhorn Museum (2013-10-07), a sticker with no text (2015-07-30), and four remarks of 2018 on unrelated subjects or about the critic. None of these is earlier than an item already held for the same title or phrase. What they add is continuity: 'Art Market Reform' is in public use under the studio principal's name in every year from 2012 to 2016, and 'What Hedge Funds ?!' and 'Metaconceptual Art' recur alongside it. The comment of 2018-10-09 was written four days after the Banksy painting was shredded in Sotheby's London saleroom on 2018-10-05, and two days before the comments of 2018-10-11 set out in the record of the 2018 comments. The export does not preserve the photograph it answered, so what it refers to is not established, and this record does not say that it concerns that event. As with the comments above, only the studio principal's words are quoted, the critic is identified by role only, and the source is the same comments file, with the checksum given in the evidence-status note." .
_:r15b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r15b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r15b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Privacy. The art critic whose posts carried the comments is identified by role only, and the private correspondents are not named; nothing any of them wrote is reproduced. Only the studio principal's words are quoted. The Facebook page named in the message of 2013-05-29, facebook.com/ArtMarketReform, and the page the message of 2012-11-25 describes as newly started are not held, and the Internet Archive holds no capture of either from those years." .
_:r15b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r15b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r15b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r15b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r15b9 .
_:r15b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E65_Creation> .
_:r15b8 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compilation of the 2012-2013 Facebook and USA Projects evidence record" .
_:r15b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r15b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
