_:r36b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "record:priority-live-auction-2009" .
_:r36b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r36b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r36b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Supporting documentation is described at evidence-live-auction-2009 and includes 2008 Sotheby's correspondence and the public catalogue lot. Recommended framing: the artist's asserted conceptual designation of an auction engagement. Avoided claims: 'first in history', publicly witnessed live creation, or precedence over any later artist or event, absent independent recognition and separately published evidence." .
_:r36b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r36b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r36b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The phrase 'made explicit over time' can now be given its earliest located date. On 2013-09-12 the studio principal set the designation down in writing to a university art museum, naming the Sotheby's lot and calling the consignment a performance act of Metaconceptual Art. That letter is the earliest articulation of this claim delivered to an institution, and the earliest to call the sale Metaconceptual Art; it is the artist's own declaration, and it postdates the 2009 engagement by four years. An earlier statement that the sale was a work survives in a private message of 2010-04-12, dated by Facebook's servers, in which the studio principal calls the sale 'an act of contemporary conceptual art', thirteen months after the sale. It too is the artist's own statement, and it does not use the word Metaconceptual." .
_:r36b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r36b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
