_:r39b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r39b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r39b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The public page treated as the artwork: a surface where language, navigation, metadata, revision, and viewing conditions become material. The website is one of the work's forms, not a container for it." .
_:r39b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r39b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r39b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r39b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r39b4 .
_:r39b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E65_Creation> .
_:r39b3 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Creation of The Website Itself" .
_:r39b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r39b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r39b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r39b4 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2026" .
_:r3b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Art Tax" .
_:r3b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r3b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r3b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r3b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:art-tax" .
_:r3b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r3b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r3b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A work of Metaconceptual Art titled by Sun & Rain Works and named, with Art Market Reform, in the studio's letter of 2013-09-12 to the Jordan Schnitzer Museum of Art: a proposal that art sales be taxed, advanced on the local, state, national and international levels, to press for accountability, transparency and regulation in the art market. The studio states, on 2026-09-22, that the work exists and is held in its own collection. The letter remains the only source for it published here, and no image, text or other material of the work is published with this record." .
_:r3b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r3b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r3b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Why this record exists, and how thin it is. This work was absent from the collection until 2026-09-22, although the studio had named it to an institution in 2013 in the same sentence as Art Market Reform, which has had a record throughout. The omission was this collection's. The record is created so that the work the letter names is addressable, and it is thin because of what this collection holds rather than because of what exists: a title, a one-sentence account of the proposal taken from the letter's own words, and the letter as its only source." .
_:r3b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r3b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r3b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What the letter says, in its own words. It introduces the pair: 'Two popular examples of Metaconceptual Art, which are ongoing through time and space as well, are titled \"Art Market Reform\" , and \"Art Tax\"'. Under the first of the two it sets out what both are for: 'Promoting Art Tax on the local, state, national, and international levels to encourage and promote accountability, transparency, and regulation in the Art Market and Art World.' It states that the goal is 'to begin, encourage, and promote an open discussion' about them, and that a proposal for both had been submitted to the White House two days earlier. The last of these is the studio's report of its own act; no acknowledgement, reply or filing has been produced, and this collection does not assert that the proposal was received or read." .
_:r3b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r3b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r3b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What is not held, stated so that nobody infers more than there is. This collection holds no image of the work, no text of the proposal, no correspondence about it other than the 2013 letter, and nothing from any year before 2013 that carries the title. The work's dating is therefore an attestation and not a creation date: the title was in use on 2013-09-12, and the letter's own phrase, that the works are 'ongoing through time and space', describes something continuing rather than finished. No creation event is recorded here for that reason. That question is no longer open in one direction. The studio states, on 2026-09-22, that the work exists and is held in its collection, so the thinness of this record is a fact about what has been published here and not about what exists. The statement is the studio's, about its own holdings, and nobody outside the studio has examined the work; no medium, support, measurement or date of making has been supplied, and none is recorded. When the object's particulars and a photograph of it are to hand, this record should describe the object and be replaced by a fuller one." .
_:r3b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r3b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r40b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sotheby's Photographs auction (sale N08533, 2009)" .
