_:r40b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "activity:sothebys-photographs-auction-2009" .
_:r40b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r40b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r40b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2009-03-30T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r40b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2009-03-30T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r40b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r40b2 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "30 March 2009" .
_:r40b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The public Sotheby's Photographs auction (sale N08533), New York, 2009, carried out by Sotheby's, at which Sun & Rain Works consigned an Ansel Adams photograph, 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks' (lot 16). Sun & Rain Works designates its engagement with this auction as the material of the concept of the auction as artwork, realised in the works www.wtfisart.com and WTF is Ansel Adams. This record names the real-world event and cites the public catalogue; it does not assert that Sotheby's authored, endorsed, or participated in the artwork, and the catalogue does not name Sun & Rain Works." .
_:r40b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r40b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r40b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E53_Place> .
_:r40b4 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sotheby's, New York" .
_:r41b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sotheby's" .
_:r41b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r41b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r41b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r41b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "agent:sothebys" .
_:r41b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r41b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r41b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "https://www.sothebys.com/" .
_:r41b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404626> .
_:r41b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r41b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "International auction house founded in 1744. Named here only as the institution that carried out the Sotheby's Photographs auction (sale N08533), New York, 2009 — the public event that Sun & Rain Works designates as the material of the concept of the auction as artwork, realised in the works www.wtfisart.com and WTF is Ansel Adams. Recording Sotheby's as the auction's host asserts no partnership, endorsement, or claim against Sotheby's." .
_:r41b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r41b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r42b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sun & Rain Works" .
_:r42b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r42b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r42b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r42b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "agent:sun-and-rain-works" .
_:r42b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r42b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r42b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The art business and studio established in 2005 that authors Metaconceptual Art and holds its copyright." .
_:r42b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r42b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r42b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The name. The studio principal's own gloss on the name, 'It takes Sun and Rain to make a Rainbow', is first dated in a private Facebook message of 2009-10-16 and recurs in 2012; it is set out in the record of the 2009 Facebook evidence." .
_:r42b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r42b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r42b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The studio's own accounts of when the business began, and of a break in it. The business's earliest attestation in this collection is a third party's: the Eugene Saturday Market's records of its membership in 2005, 2006 and 2008, on which the formation date given here rests. The studio principal's own statements place the start differently. In a private Facebook message of 2012-11-25 at 14:16 UTC, by Facebook's clock, written a day or two after he set up the business's Facebook page, he wrote 'S & R W started 4+ years ago, although the fb page is only 24-48 hours old', which on its own terms points to about 2008; in the same exchange he wrote that 'Much of the Art S & R W makes is VERY Traditional. i.e. drawing, painting, sculpture, collage, etc.' In another private message, of 2014-10-23, he wrote that he was 'trying to find balance and restart my art business \"Sun and Rain Works\"', which implies that the business had lapsed for a time before late 2014. Neither statement contradicts the market's record, which is the firmer source because it is a third party's; they are recorded because they are the studio's own words at the time, and they describe the business as starting later than, and as interrupted after, the formation date given here. The correspondents are not named, and only the studio principal's words are quoted. The two threads' files in the account data have SHA-256 1d3b2a20d85b4ac622e22750db44b1e758e777a65fe505577f9f5b95a0695993 and 0f76ab2dcdfc826815eeef44336033e109065d4ebc6e420ed5a752ff51ac3a7c, within the archive facebook-joechirum-2026-09-24-TZ87gGfq.zip, SHA-256 c978c3bd338a6a9a934d3aa05a81d2c298c49200bf7e4edc98b8329c02103097." .
_:r42b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r42b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r42b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r42b6 .
_:r42b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E66_Formation> .
_:r42b5 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Formation of Sun & Rain Works" .
_:r42b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2005-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r42b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2005-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r42b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r42b6 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2005" .
_:r43b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What Hedge Funds ?!" .
_:r43b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r43b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r43b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r43b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:what-hedge-funds" .
_:r43b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r43b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r43b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A painting by Sun & Rain Works carrying the words 'what hedge funds ?' in painted letters. It is known to this collection from one photograph, which the studio published on its own website and which the Internet Archive captured on 2014-12-18 and again on 2016-01-11. No image of the painting is published with this record, and no medium, support, measurement or date of making is recorded, because none has been supplied." .
_:r43b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r43b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r43b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "How it is dated, and how far that reaches. The photograph sits on the studio's site at sites/all/themes/corporateclean/mockup/slide-3.jpg and is held by the Internet Archive at https://web.archive.org/web/20141218140553id_/http://wtfisart.com/sites/all/themes/corporateclean/mockup/slide-3.jpg, 86,711 bytes, 500 by 250 pixels. Above it the site's slider reads 'What Hedge Funds ?! invest in Art'. What that establishes is that the painting existed and had been photographed by 2014-12-18, on the evidence of a third party with no stake in this collection, and that it was still on the site on 2016-01-11. What it does not establish is when the painting was made, which the capture cannot reach, or anything about the object itself beyond what a banner-shaped crop shows." .
_:r43b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r43b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r43b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What is not held. This collection holds no photograph of the painting other than the archived crop, which is 500 by 250 pixels and therefore a detail rather than documentation of the whole work. It holds no measurement, no statement of medium, no record of where the painting is, and nothing dated before 2014 that carries the title. The studio has stated, in 2026, that its works exist and are held in its own collection; that statement covers this one no more and no less than the others, and nobody outside the studio has examined it. If the painting is photographed and measured, this record should be replaced by a fuller one." .
_:r43b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r43b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r44b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P15_was_influenced_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/auction-as-artwork> .
_:r44b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r44b1 .
_:r44b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by> _:r44b2 .
_:r44b0 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P9i_forms_part_of> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/production-live-auction-2009> .
_:r44b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E12_Production> .
_:r44b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Designation of WTF is Ansel Adams" .
