_:r44b1 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2009-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r44b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r44b1 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2009" .
_:r44b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A work in its own right. Earlier versions of this record modelled WTF is Ansel Adams as a part of a titled work, 'The Auction as Artwork'. There was no such titled work; that phrase names the concept the studio's two works around the 2009 engagement share, and the correction is set out in the record for that concept. This work is recorded as a work, related to www.wtfisart.com, and its making is recorded as influenced by the concept rather than as a part of it. The origin claim for 2009 names www.wtfisart.com as its work and this one as the related work, because the website's name is independently dated and this work's title is not: the public uses of the title held here are an undated profile biography and a public Facebook comment of 2018-10-11, nine and a half years after the sale and made in answer to that day's news of Banksy's 'Love is in the Bin', which gives the title with the year 2009; the comment dates the title to 2018, not to 2009, and is set out in the record of the 2018 comments." .
_:r44b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r44b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The work is Sun & Rain Works' conceptual designation connected to the consignment of lot 16 at Sotheby's Photographs, 2009; it is an assertion by the artist and is not recorded as a publicly witnessed performance." .
_:r44b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r44b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b3 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Artwork page" .
_:r44b3 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/digitally_carried_by> _:r44b4 .
_:r44b4 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "text/html" .
_:r44b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMdig/D1_Digital_Object> .
_:r44b4 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metaconceptual Art — WTF is Ansel Adams" .
_:r44b4 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/access_point> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/artworks#work-wtf-is-ansel-adams> .
_:r44b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "WTF is Ansel Adams" .
_:r44b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r44b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r44b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r44b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:wtf-is-ansel-adams" .
_:r44b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r44b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r44b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A Metaconceptual Art work that Sun & Rain Works designates around its consignment of the Ansel Adams photograph 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks' (lot 16) to Sotheby's Photographs, 2009 (sale N08533, New York). Titled as a play on the auction and the canonical name of Ansel Adams, it treats the act of bringing the photograph to auction — its lot, its authority, its attribution — as the material of a conceptual work, alongside the born-digital work www.wtfisart.com. The work is a designation asserted by the artist and made explicit over time; it is not recorded as a publicly witnessed performance, and the Sotheby's catalogue lists the lot as an Ansel Adams photograph without naming Sun & Rain Works." .
_:r44b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r44b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Documentation reported by Sun & Rain Works includes 2008 correspondence with Sotheby's Photographs, the public catalogue lot, photographs, and related records; these evidence the artist identity and the consignment. The fuller archive remains held by the studio pending redaction and rights review. This record asserts no historical-priority or precedence claim absent separately published evidence." .
_:r44b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r44b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r44b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What the W stands for, in the artist's account. The studio states, in 2026, that the W of this title stands for 'Who', so that it reads 'Who the F is Ansel Adams', while the W of the companion work www.wtfisart.com stands for 'What'. No document from 2008 or 2009 spells out either expansion; this collection searched the correspondence of those years and the studio's working files and found none. The reading is the artist's and is recorded as that. What the choice does can be stated without adding to it: 'What' is the ordinary word of the idiom, so the companion work asks what art is, and 'Who' bends the idiom, so this work asks instead about a person - who the photographer is, and so what his name, stamp and signature do to a print whose identity rests on them. That gloss is this collection's and not the artist's." .
_:r44b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r44b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Artwork page" .
_:r45b0 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/digitally_carried_by> _:r45b1 .
_:r45b1 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "text/html" .
_:r45b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMdig/D1_Digital_Object> .
_:r45b1 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metaconceptual Art — www.wtfisart.com Reconstruction" .
_:r45b1 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/access_point> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/artworks/wtfisart-reconstruction> .
_:r45b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r45b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r45b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r45b10 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2026" .
_:r45b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "www.wtfisart.com — Reconstruction" .
_:r45b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r45b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r45b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r45b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:wtfisart-reconstruction" .
_:r45b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r45b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r45b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A nine-page website built in 2026 that reconstructs www.wtfisart.com, the site Sun & Rain Works says it made in 2009, from the only two things that survive of it: the WTFIA folder of source documents assembled for it, and Growing Aloha, an unrelated website built by the same hands in the same months whose HTML, stylesheet and Dreamweaver template are intact. The content is WTFIA's; the form is Growing Aloha's. It is published as a work in its own right and is labelled as a reconstruction on every page." .
_:r45b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r45b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What is transcribed, and what is inferred. Transcribed from the 2009 documents, unchanged: twenty-four dated press reports on the art market spanning 2000 to 2009, twenty-two of them carrying the source link the compiler recorded, with their headlines, bylines and excerpts; sixty-four Old Master dealers and galleries, each with the web address recorded for it in 2009; eighty-one modern and contemporary galleries grouped by state and country, for which the source document holds no web addresses; and a one-page note on the photographer Lee Balterman. Inferred, and belonging to the reconstruction rather than to 2009: the division into pages, the page titles, the order of the navigation column, the wording of the front page, the colour palette, and the existence of a page about the Ansel Adams consignment. Nothing in the surviving material records how the 2009 pages were arranged or what they said." .
_:r45b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r45b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "How the form was derived. Growing Aloha, held on the same medium as the WTFIA folder and dated 2009-01-16 to 2009-01-20, is a Dreamweaver site built on the 'three column liquid, header and footer' starter layout: XHTML 1.0 Transitional, a .dwt template with named editable and repeating regions, the layout stylesheet inline in a style element wrapped in HTML comments, an Internet Explorer conditional comment supplying the hasLayout zoom fix, an external stylesheet of content-named classes, and a left column of block-display anchor links. Every one of those traits is reproduced here, and the reconstruction's stylesheet is modelled directly on Aloha.css, class for class. The reconstruction's own pages are valid XHTML 1.0 Transitional and carry Dreamweaver template-instance markers naming a template, Templates/WTFIA.dwt, which is published alongside them." .
_:r45b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r45b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What was deliberately omitted. The 2009 sibling carried a Google Custom Search box and three AdSense units, and the surviving code contains the studio's own publisher and partner identifiers; the live third-party script and those identifiers are not reproduced, and the slots are marked where they sat. The art-historical plates and art-market press pictures in the WTFIA folder are third-party material held back pending rights review and are not shown. The 2009 photographs documenting the Ansel Adams print in the storage unit show an identifiable person and are withheld pending consent; the single photograph reproduced, the print's verso, is the studio's own and was already published. Growing Aloha's tiled background photograph belongs to an unrelated project and is not carried over. The press excerpts that are shown are short passages reproduced for commentary, each attributed to its author and publication and linked to its source." .
_:r45b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r45b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Scope. This is a reconstruction and is evidence of nothing about the 2009 website beyond what the source documents already evidence. It is not a recovered copy: no HTML from www.wtfisart.com survives in the studio's archive or is known to exist elsewhere, and the WTFIA evidence record states that the folder holds what was made for the site rather than what the site published. It does not show that the site went live in 2009. The earliest Internet Archive capture of the domain, from February 2011, is a parked advertising page, which is evidence about February 2011 and not about 2009: the registrar's receipts show a one-year registration taken on 2009-03-16 and no renewal of it in the year that followed, so by February 2011 the domain had lapsed, and a parked page is what a registrar commonly serves at a lapsed address. The same receipts show the studio registering the name again on 2011-10-16, eight months after that capture, which bears on what became of the domain afterwards and not on what stood at it in 2009. What those receipts do establish is that the domain existed and was hosted from 2009-03-16; what stood at it in 2009, if anything, is evidenced by nothing. The studio's account that this site and the Sotheby's consignment were companion works is recorded as the artist's account: the dates are consistent with it, the latest material in the folder having been last saved a week before the sale, but no document in the folder mentions the consignment, and consistency is not intent. No precedence over any other artist, work, or event is claimed." .
_:r45b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r45b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r45b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r45b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P16_used_specific_object> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-wtfia-2009> .
_:r45b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r45b10 .
_:r45b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E65_Creation> .
_:r45b9 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Creation of the www.wtfisart.com reconstruction" .
_:r46b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Artwork page" .
_:r46b0 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/digitally_carried_by> _:r46b1 .
_:r46b1 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "text/html" .
_:r46b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMdig/D1_Digital_Object> .
_:r46b1 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metaconceptual Art - www.wtfisart.com" .
_:r46b1 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/access_point> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/artworks/wtfisart> .
_:r46b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What the W stands for, in the artist's account. The studio states, in 2026, that the W of this work's name stands for 'What', so that it reads 'What the F is Art', while the W of the companion work WTF is Ansel Adams stands for 'Who'. No document from 2008 or 2009 spells out the expansion, and the reading is recorded as the artist's. It is consistent with the double reading recorded above: 'What' is the idiom's ordinary word, and the name is both the question what art is and the statement that it is that." .
_:r46b10 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b11 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The work of the 2009 origin claim. This collection's origin claim for the 2009 engagement previously named a titled work, 'The Auction as Artwork', of which this website was modelled as an associated part. There was no such titled work, and the correction is set out in the record for the concept. The claim now names www.wtfisart.com, as the better dated of the studio's two works around the engagement: the registrar's receipt of 2009-03-16, billed to Sun and Rain Works, fixes the name fourteen days before the sale, on a document the studio did not write. WTF is Ansel Adams is recorded as the related work." .
_:r46b11 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b12 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
_:r46b12 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P15_was_influenced_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/auction-as-artwork> .
_:r46b12 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span> _:r46b13 .
_:r46b12 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by> _:r46b14 .
_:r46b12 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P9i_forms_part_of> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/production-live-auction-2009> .
_:r46b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E65_Creation> .
_:r46b12 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Creation of www.wtfisart.com" .
_:r46b13 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82a_begin_of_the_begin> "2009-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r46b13 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P82b_end_of_the_end> "2009-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:r46b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span> .
_:r46b13 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2009" .
_:r46b14 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The website was built by Sun & Rain Works around 2009 in connection with its Sotheby's Photographs auction engagement; it is not recorded as having been authored live in the auction room." .
_:r46b14 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "www.wtfisart.com" .
_:r46b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r46b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r46b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r46b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:wtfisart" .
_:r46b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r46b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r46b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "https://www.wtfisart.com/" .
_:r46b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404626> .
_:r46b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r46b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A born-digital Metaconceptual Art work: a website built and owned by Sun & Rain Works around 2009, in connection with its Sotheby's Photographs auction engagement (sale N08533). Sun & Rain Works designates it as a work realising the concept of the auction as artwork." .
_:r46b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "www.wtfisart.com is associated by Sun & Rain Works with the concept of the auction as artwork, in which Sun & Rain Works designates its 2009 Sotheby's Photographs auction engagement as art. The designation is an assertion by the artist." .
_:r46b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Sun & Rain Works reports domain-registration and hosting receipts, site metadata, and related records documenting the website's existence and date. The fuller archive remains held by the studio pending redaction and rights review." .
_:r46b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "What the public record of the domain shows, checked 2026-09-01. The Verisign registry gives wtfisart.com a registration event of 2024-08-29 under the handle 2912143398_DOMAIN_COM-VRSN, with nameservers at a shared hosting provider. A renewal does not reset a creation date, so a registration event of that date on a freshly issued handle means the domain lapsed at some earlier point and was registered again as a new object. The consequence is that the original creation date is no longer in the public registry and cannot be recovered from it. The Internet Archive's earliest capture of the domain is of 2010-01-25 16:15:12 UTC, and the address answered not with a page but with a redirect, sent by a web server that named itself as serving wtfisart.com, to a generic page on securepaynet.net, a domain of the registrar's hosting service. A hosting account for the domain therefore existed in January 2010, but it served no studio content, which agrees with the registrar's receipts, on which the monthly hosting payments for the site run to 2009-12-15. The next capture, of 2011-02-10 21:34:22 UTC, is a parked advertising page carrying no studio content, which is what a registrar commonly serves at an address whose registration has lapsed. Neither capture shows what the site carried in 2009. An earlier version of this record gave the 2011 capture as the earliest; that rested on a look-up of the home page's address alone, and a search of every address under the domain, made on 2026-09-24, found the redirect of 2010. The studio was not the first to register the name. The free view of a commercial DNS-history service, CompleteDNS, consulted on 2026-09-25, records wtfisart.com as created in the week of 2002-08-02 to 2002-08-08, with name servers at idirections.com, and as dropped between 2002-08-09 and 2003-01-02; a second service, DomainTools, reports historical WHOIS records for the name beginning 2001-04-30, whose content was not examined. Who held the name then is not shown and was not sought, nothing indicates that a website existed at the address, and no web archive holds a capture of it before 2010. The studio's registration of 2009-03-16 was an ordinary new registration of a name then available, not a purchase of an existing one. The remainder of both services' histories is behind a subscription and was not consulted. The date the studio first registered this domain is therefore not recoverable from the registry, but it is no longer undetermined: the registrar's own receipts, described in the hosting-receipts record, give a registration of WTFISART.COM on 2009-03-16 at 00:45:06 UTC and hosting bought for it the same night, with that hosting paid monthly to at least 2009-12-15. Those are a third party's business records rather than the studio's assertion. What stood at the address in 2009 remains unevidenced." .
_:r46b8 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r46b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The name reads two ways. Written without spaces or punctuation, wtfisart is both a question, 'WTF is art?', and a statement, 'WTF is art'. The studio holds, in its account given in 2026, that the double reading was deliberate and that registering the name declared the work art. The registrar's receipt of 2009-03-16, billed to Sun and Rain Works, independently dates the name; the intent is the studio's statement, and the hosting-receipts record sets out the distinction." .
_:r46b9 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r46b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r4b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r4b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Artwork page" .
_:r4b0 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/digitally_carried_by> _:r4b1 .
_:r4b1 <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "text/html" .
_:r4b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ics.forth.gr/isl/CRMdig/D1_Digital_Object> .
_:r4b1 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metaconceptual Art — The auction as artwork (concept)" .
_:r4b1 <https://linked.art/ns/terms/access_point> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/artworks#work-auction-as-artwork> .
_:r4b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The auction as artwork (concept)" .
_:r4b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670> .
_:r4b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P72_has_language> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300388277> .
_:r4b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation> .
_:r4b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "work:auction-as-artwork" .
_:r4b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r4b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r4b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A correction to what this record is. Until 2026-09-22 this collection recorded 'The Auction as Artwork' as a titled work, and modelled the two works around the 2009 engagement as its parts. The studio has stated that there was never a work of that title: the works are WTF is Ansel Adams and www.wtfisart.com, and the auction as artwork is the concept they share. The records agree with the studio. The phrase first appears in this collection on 2026-07-10, in the commit that first modelled the engagement, and no dated document uses it - not the 2008 and 2009 correspondence, not the private message of 2010, not the postings of 2011 and 2012, not the studio's archived websites, and not the 2013 letter to a university museum, which calls the sale 'a performance act of Metaconceptual Art' and gives it no title at all. The title was therefore this collection's, introduced by its data model, and not the artist's. The record keeps its identifier, because that identifier has been published, cited and archived, and is retyped from a made object to a concept. Two consequences follow. The origin claim for 2009 now names www.wtfisart.com as its work, the better dated of the two, whose name the registrar dates to 2009-03-16, fourteen days before the sale; WTF is Ansel Adams is recorded as the related work. And nothing about what is evidenced changes: the concept remains the studio's assertion, and its earliest dated statement is now a private message of 2010-04-12, dated by Facebook's servers, in which the studio principal calls the sale 'an act of contemporary conceptual art' and gives it no title." .
_:r4b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r4b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r4b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The letter that gives the auction no title gives two other works one. The correction above rests in part on the 2013 letter to a university museum, which describes the sale as 'a performance act of Metaconceptual Art' and gives it no title. That is worth more than an absence, because the same letter titles other work in the same breath: 'Two popular examples of Metaconceptual Art, which are ongoing through time and space as well, are titled \"Art Market Reform\" , and \"Art Tax\"'. So the writer was naming works when he had names for them, in his own words, four years after the sale, and did not name this one. The argument for this record is therefore not only that no document uses the phrase 'The Auction as Artwork'; it is that the one document in which the studio lists its titled works, and mentions the auction, titles the works and not the auction." .
_:r4b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r4b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r4b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A concept of Sun & Rain Works, and not a work, formed in connection with the Sotheby's Photographs auction of 2009 (sale N08533, New York), at which Sun & Rain Works consigned an Ansel Adams photograph, 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks' (lot 16). Following the logic of the readymade, Sun & Rain Works frames its engagement with that public institutional event — its mechanism of value, authority, and sale — as the material of art. This is a designation asserted by the artist and made explicit over time; it is not a publicly witnessed live-creation event, and the Sotheby's catalogue does not name Sun & Rain Works. The concept is realised in two works, the website www.wtfisart.com and WTF is Ansel Adams; it is not itself a titled work, and the correction above sets out how this collection came to record it as one." .
_:r4b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r4b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r4b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Documentation reported by Sun & Rain Works includes 2008 correspondence with Sotheby's Photographs, the public catalogue lot, photographs, receipts, and related records; these evidence the artist identity and the consignment. The fuller archive remains held by the studio pending redaction and rights review. This record makes no adjudicated historical-priority claim and asserts no comparison with, or precedence over, any later artist or event absent separately published evidence." .
_:r4b7 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r4b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
