_:r8b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r8b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "A canonical eight-sentence proposition set framing Metaconceptual Art as a field of form, institution, market, history, medium, access, and life. Written after Sol LeWitt's Sentences on Conceptual Art." .
_:r8b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r8b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r8b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The sequence has a documented public form predating this site by fourteen years. It was posted in full, as 'The 8 Defining characteristics of Metaconceptual Art', on 2012-11-22, twenty-three days after a private Facebook message of 2012-10-30 that refers to the eight characteristics without listing them, and the text published here agrees with that posting word for word apart from a comma, a space, and the spelling of 'Transcendance', since normalised. The posting is described in the 2011-2012 posting evidence record. The stated debt to Sol LeWitt does not appear in the 2012 text and is a later framing." .
